    "title": "Oconee County sets Meet the Teacher before new school year begins - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Wayne Ford ,\n20 hours ago\nThe first day of school for the Oconee County School District is barely a month away.\nThe school system is preparing a way for students to get acquainted with their new teachers and classrooms before the official first day begins on Aug. 3.\nHelping Others: Blood drive set July 9 at Piedmont Athens amid shortages\nThe district announced recently that it will host Meet the Teacher on July 30 to help acquaint students with the 2026-27 school year. The times were spaced out to accommodate families and reduce traffic, school officials said.\nThe elementary schools will greet those families with last names beginning with A through H from 8:30 a.m. to 9:30 a.m. Then I through Q from 9:30 a.m. to 10:30 a.m., and R through Z meets from 10:30 a.m. to 11:30 a.m.\nThe middle schools will use the same letter format and times. The high schools, grades 9-12, will host the day from 1-3 p.m.\nThis article originally appeared on Athens Banner-Herald: Oconee County sets Meet the Teacher before new school year begins\n1",
    "summary": "The school system is preparing a way for students to get acquainted with their new teachers and classrooms before the official first day begins on Aug. 3. Helping Others: Blood drive set July 9 at Piedmont Athens amid shortages The district announced recently that it will host Meet the Teacher on July 30 to help acquaint students with the 2026-27 school year. The times were spaced out to accommodate families and reduce traffic, school officials said.",
